Q: Is there a way to generate a train of gaussian pulses distanced by a certain PRT for a radar system? A: <p>Given a single pulse and a PRT, PRT being the inverse of PRF Pulse Repetition Frequency MATLAB has the command <code>pulstran</code> precisely to generate trains of pulses :</p>
<p>Example 1</p>
<pre><code>fs = 100e9; % Sample rate
t = 0 : 1/fs : 2500/fs; % Time vector
D = [2.5 10 17.5]' * 1e-9; % Delays in seconds
w = 1e-9; % Pulse width
y = pulstran(t, D, @rectpuls, w); % Rectangular pulse train
plot(t, y); title('Rectangular Pulse Train');
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/O9IbyfG1.jpg" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/O9IbyfG1.jpg" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
<p>Example 2</p>
<pre><code>t = 0:1/1e3:60;
d = [0:2:60;sin(2*pi*0.05*(0:2:60))]';
x = @rectpuls;
y = pulstran(t,d,x);
plot(t,y)

hold off
xlabel('Time (s)')
ylabel('Waveform')
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/wjL0SZoY.jpg" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/wjL0SZoY.jpg" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
<p>Example 3</p>
<pre><code>fs = 1e3;
t = 0:1/1e3:1;
d = 0:1/3:1;   
x = tripuls(t,0.2,-1);
y = pulstran(t,d,x,fs);

plot(t,y)
hold off
xlabel('Time (s)')
ylabel('Waveform')
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/gXqySCIz.jpg" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/gXqySCIz.jpg" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
<p>Example 4:</p>
<pre><code>fs = 1e7;
tc = gauspuls('cutoff',10e3,0.5,[],-40); 
t = -tc:1/fs:tc; 
x = gauspuls(t,10e3,0.5); 
plot(t,x)
xlabel('Time (s)')
ylabel('Waveform')
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/EDMSVIGZ.jpg" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/EDMSVIGZ.jpg" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
<pre><code>ts = 0:1/50e3:0.025;
d = [0:1/1e3:0.025;sin(2*pi*0.1*(0:25))]';
y = pulstran(ts,d,x,fs);
Plot the periodic Gaussian pulse train.

plot(ts,y)
xlim([0 0.01])
xlabel('Time (s)')
ylabel('Waveform')
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://i.sstatic.net/19ac4H13.jpg" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/19ac4H13.jpg" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>
